# etude-5dr.4 final review

ANCESTOR: etude-5dr (P1) — GitHub issue #15 and a blocked downstream project
require caller-CWD producing runners and their fail-closed mutation guard to ship
together in one pull request.

BLAST RADIUS: 13 repository files spanning workflow schema, live-run execution,
manifest audit/versioning, CLI rendering/wiring, tests, and shipped run/gate docs.
Verification builds only this worktree and creates disposable Git repositories.
No package install, shared service, main-branch push, or external mutation is
performed before the requested branch/PR publication.

TRUST BOUNDARY: workflow configuration, the installed Git executable, canonical
repository identity, and configured Git normalization/ignore/file-mode semantics
are trusted. The authorized runner is trusted not to rewrite those semantics or
Git control files solely to alter inspection. Ordinary runner output and tracked,
index, and non-ignored untracked effects are untrusted until the postflight passes.
Hostile same-process replacement of Git/tooling and unrelated concurrent writers
are outside the contract; caller mode requires exclusive working-tree access.

TOPOLOGY: one engine synchronously invokes one producing runner at the single
`runAndCaptureStage` site shared by fresh and resumed runs. No second caller-mode
invoker exists; gate checks and seats remain hermetic.

DURABILITY CLASS: caller-runner effects are at-least-once until stage publication;
successful publication remains the existing CAS-protected ref append. The
AUTHORITATIVE generation identity is the stable post-run Git commit SHA, not the
invocation SHA, ancestry relationship, or a timestamp proxy.

IRREVERSIBLE SEQUENCE caller-runner: 1 steps
IRREVERSIBLE STEP caller-runner.1: invoke the authorized producing runner in the caller working tree

Crash residual: runner edits or a clean commit may survive without a stage record;
resume is at-least-once, so the operator reconciles the live tree first and caller
runners must be repeat-safe.

## Outcome

- `runner.workspace` supports opt-in `caller`; absent/`hermetic` keeps the
  detached worktree and stage/default/CLI override precedence is tested.
- The CLI passes its exact invocation directory only to caller producing runners.
- The same repository-wide inspection runs before and after the runner: caller
  repository identity must match, tracked gitlinks and hidden index flags are
  rejected, and staged/unstaged/non-ignored-untracked status must be empty.
- Preflight rejects valuable dirty or hidden work before runner invocation.
  Postflight resolves a stable authoritative HEAD before any artifact storage,
  manifest append, gate check, or seat execution.
- Clean commits and intentional history rewrites are allowed; manifest v4 records
  `runner_workspace: caller` and the exact post-run SHA. Legacy hermetic manifest
  versions remain unchanged and reject the new field below v4.
- Gate checks and seats remain on the original pinned hermetic checkout.

